From c60a74fdc84ad6b048c6169ca25758827827dac4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tawheed Makhdoomi <_@tawheed.cc>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:15:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 36/41] WIP: media: i2c: ov7251: enable the strobe output
 (Surface Pro X IR emitter)

On the Surface Pro X the face-authentication IR emitter is switched by
the OV7251 STROBE pin, not by the PMIC flash LED block: with the strobe
registers set as the Windows sensor module does (0x3005 = 0x08,
0x3b81 = 0xaa, 0x3b8b = 0x00, 0x3b8e/8f = 0x03/0x08, 0x3b94/95 =
0x05/0xf2, 0x3b96 = 0xc0) the scene is lit during exposure; the driver's
defaults leave the strobe output disabled and the image dark.

Hardcoded in the mode tables for now; needs a proper control or DT
property before it can go upstream.

